From e7bbc90a10168619a5443bd5da25eb940b9bcfe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:10:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] language: the help of the Dolby Vision transport, as composed
 by default

The help of "Transport" (core and Estuary, en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx) names
"As composed" as the default and says in plain words what the IPT choice
measured. The notes for translators no longer call IPT the default.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po         | 4 ++--
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po             | 4 ++--
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po             | 6 +++---
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po             | 6 +++---
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po             | 6 +++---
 5 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 5bbeece..08da77e 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -25923,7 +25923,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport"; translated in Estuary (#32001)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39895"
-msgid "For experts. How native Dolby Vision is sent to the TV. As licensed players send (IPT), the default: the picture the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 builds, converted to IPT-PQ-c2 for profiles 7 and 8, as licensed players are reported to send every profile (profile 5 is IPT already); where a graphics chip cannot keep up, the automatic fidelity step-down sends it as composed at its last level. As composed: that picture as it is, in the colour representation the video describes (YCbCr, or IPT for profile 5). Converted to BT.2020: the picture is rebuilt in RGB and converted to BT.2020 YCbCr, as earlier builds sent it, to compare on a display. Menus or subtitles drawn over the video are converted into the representation that is sent. What the step-down finds is not kept while Converted to BT.2020 is chosen. Takes effect from the next video."
+msgid "For experts. How native Dolby Vision is sent to the TV. As composed, the default: the picture the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 builds, exactly as it is, in the colour representation the video describes (YCbCr, or IPT for profile 5). As licensed players send (IPT): profiles 7 and 8 converted to IPT-PQ-c2, as licensed players are reported to send them (where a graphics chip cannot keep up, it goes out as composed). It measured a little less faithful: the TV gives the right pixel of each pair the colour worked out for the left one, which shows where the light changes sharply inside a strong colour. Converted to BT.2020: the picture is rebuilt in RGB and converted to BT.2020 YCbCr, as earlier builds sent it, to compare on a display. Menus or subtitles drawn over the video are converted into the representation that is sent. What the step-down finds is not kept while Converted to BT.2020 is chosen. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport": the composer's picture as it is, as clause 6 of ETSI GS CCM 001 describes (the default); also on the Dolby Vision page of the player information; translated in Estuary (#32002)
@@ -25939,7 +25939,7 @@ msgid "Converted to BT.2020"
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport": the composer's picture in IPT-PQ-c2, as licensed players are reported to send it (the default); also on the Dolby Vision page of the player information; translated in Estuary (#32006)
+#. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport": the composer's picture in IPT-PQ-c2, as licensed players are reported to send it (an expert choice); also on the Dolby Vision page of the player information; translated in Estuary (#32006)
 msgctxt "#39898"
 msgid "As licensed players send (IPT)"
 msgstr ""
